    "narrative": "With the league calendar closing in, our roster management for Ghost Ride the WHIP remains laser-focused on maximizing efficiency against the cap. Today\u2019s primary focus is **Brice Turang**, who anchors our lineup with a score of 46.03. While a matchup against Nick Pivetta and his 3.17 xERA presents a significant hurdle, **Brice Turang** holds value due to his prime spot in the heart of the order\u2014assuming he sticks in the #4 hole\u2014and a dynamic platoon advantage that offers a slight buffer against Pivetta's secondary stuff. We are effectively playing for his speed-based floor in a high-stakes environment where every stolen base is worth its weight in gold.\n\nThe most notable exclusion from today\u2019s active roster is **Dalton Rushing**, who narrowly missed the cut with a score of 33.62. While **Dalton Rushing** possesses the power profile to exploit almost any park, the combination of an elite matchup against Chris Sale and the high probability of **Dalton Rushing** batting #9 renders him a sub-optimal play for our current Roto targets. We are choosing to bench **Dalton Rushing** to prioritize game cap preservation, as the risk-to-reward ratio against an ace like Sale simply does not justify the potential depletion of our remaining daily allotment.\n\nElsewhere, the lack of activity from stalwarts like **Corbin Carroll**, **Josh Naylor**, and **James Wood** due to scheduled off-days forces us into a defensive posture. We are monitoring the status of the rest of our core\u2014including **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Seiya Suzuki**\u2014for late-breaking lineup news. Given the scarcity of stolen base threats like **Jose Caballero** and **Mickey Moniak** on our bench, we remain ready to pivot should the optimizer favor a high-volatility start from **Giancarlo Stanton** or **Isaac Paredes** if late-game weather patterns shift in hitter-friendly venues. With **Trevor Story**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Cole Young**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** also under watch, our priority remains clear: protect the WHIP and maximize efficiency.",
